# The Lean modules whose C code is compiled into the library a pool worker loads.
# One per line: the Lake package, then the module's path under that package's `.lake/build/ir`.
#
# Together they are the last step of `linarith` and `nlinarith`: the search for the numbers that close a
# goal, a simplex method over exact fractions. Mathlib is not shipped as native code, so without this the
# step runs in Lean's interpreter, where it can take most of a check's time.
#
# The fifth line is what makes the difference: it holds the copies of the search that Lean specialised for
# the types linarith uses, and those copies are the code that runs. With the first four alone nothing is
# faster. The last two are small modules those five call.
mathlib Mathlib/Tactic/Linarith/Oracle/SimplexAlgorithm/Datatypes
mathlib Mathlib/Tactic/Linarith/Oracle/SimplexAlgorithm/Gauss
mathlib Mathlib/Tactic/Linarith/Oracle/SimplexAlgorithm/SimplexAlgorithm
mathlib Mathlib/Tactic/Linarith/Oracle/SimplexAlgorithm/PositiveVector
mathlib Mathlib/Tactic/Linarith/Oracle/SimplexAlgorithm
mathlib Mathlib/Data/Ineq
batteries Batteries/Data/List/Basic
